1
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:34,800
Sabrina, Down Under is a tv movie, comedy, fantasy
film directed by Kenneth R. Koch.

2
00:06:57,600 --> 00:07:03,600
Sabrina travels to Australia's Great Barrier Reef with her best friend Gwen, a fellow witch from England, for a week-long vacation where they try to help protect a
hidden mermaid colony whose habitat is threatened by ocean pollution, and by a local marine biologist determined to find the colony as his claim to fame.

3
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:32,400
While Sabrina finds romance with a "merman" from the mermaid colony, Salem the cat finds a possible romance with
another witch-turned-into-a-cat, named Hilary, but finds Sabrina's problems interfering with his plans.

4
00:13:55,200 --> 00:14:01,200
Sabrina Spellman, played by Melissa Joan Hart.

5
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:30,000
Gwen, played by Tara Strong.

6
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:58,800
Barnaby, played by Scott Michaelson.

7
00:24:21,600 --> 00:24:27,600
Fin, played by Lindsay Sloane.

8
00:27:50,400 --> 00:27:56,400
Salem Saberhagen (voice), played by Nick Bakay.

9
00:31:19,200 --> 00:31:25,200
Dr. Julian Martin, played by Peter O'Brien.

10
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Sabrina Down Under is a 1999 American television film
produced for ABC, airing on September 26, 1999.

11
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:22,800
It is a sequel to Sabrina Goes to Rome and is a companion to
the Sabrina the Teenage Witch television series.

12
00:41:45,600 --> 00:41:51,600
The film features only two characters from the television series: teenage witch Sabrina Spellman
(played by Melissa Joan Hart), and talking cat Salem Saberhagen (voiced by Nick Bakay).

13
00:45:14,400 --> 00:45:20,400
Lindsay Sloane was also a regular actress in the television
series, but plays a different character in this film.

14
00:48:43,200 --> 00:48:49,200
Tara Charendoff reprises her role as Gwen from Sabrina Goes to Rome.

15
00:52:12,000 --> 00:52:18,000
As the film is set in Australia, none of the scenes are filmed
on the original set of the television series.

16
00:55:40,800 --> 00:55:46,800
The film was directed by Kenneth R.

17
00:59:09,600 --> 00:59:15,600
Koch, who helped to produce Sabrina Goes to Rome.

18
01:02:38,400 --> 01:02:44,400
He also directed many episodes of the television series
and was a prominent producer of the show.

19
01:06:07,200 --> 01:06:13,200
Unlike Sabrina Goes to Rome, which is included in the season 7 DVD release of the Sabrina the Teenage
Witch television series, Sabrina Down Under was not included in any of the season sets.

20
01:09:36,000 --> 01:09:42,000
It was later released on a stand-alone DVD on February 7, 2017.

21
01:13:04,800 --> 01:13:10,800
Prior to this, the film  was released on VHS.

22
01:16:33,600 --> 01:16:39,600
It is available to stream on Hulu.

23
01:20:02,400 --> 01:20:08,400
The film explores themes of witch, australia, ocean, marine biologist, mermaid.

24
01:23:31,200 --> 01:23:37,200
The tone is lighthearted.
